---
// Draft for owner review. Not legal advice; have counsel read it.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Transparency - Paul Ann Media"
  description="How Paul Ann Media makes money, how it uses AI, and what it will and won't claim."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Transparency</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate">Who we are, how we get paid, how we use AI, and what we won't claim.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate">Effective November 1, 2026.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">Who we are</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">Paul Ann Media is an AI-native media group: websites, social campaigns, marketing strategy, lead generation, content systems and AI visibility. It is a Trimmie Holdings company. Paul Ann Labs is our sister company, and HomeTimeJobs is a product we own.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">Our own products</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">We build and run our own products, starting with HomeTimeJobs. When we write about one of them, we say it's ours.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">How we get paid</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">By our clients, for the work we do for them. Nobody pays us to recommend a tool, a vendor or a platform. If that ever changes, we will say so where the recommendation appears.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">Testimonials and clients</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">We don't publish client names, logos, reviews or testimonials without the client's written permission, and we never write them ourselves.</p>

    <h2 id="ai" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">How we use AI</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate">
      <li>We use AI tools to help us research, write, design and make images. A person reviews everything before it is published, and we stand behind it as our own work.</li>
      <li>The photos on this site are AI-generated illustrations. The people and places in them are not real customers, workers or places.</li>
      <li>AI doesn't make decisions about you. People answer every inquiry.</li>
      <li>We don't use what you send us through this site to train AI models.</li>
      <li>Our pages are open to AI search tools (see robots.txt and llms.txt) so they can describe us accurately.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">Client data: we only put a client's information into AI tools the client has approved in writing, and never into tools that train on it.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">Ask through the form on our <a href="/privacy/#contact" class="font-semibold text-teal-ink hover:underline">privacy page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
